# Round 18, C3-7 (fixed). E §3.2: the law-date class is bounded by "the governs spans of the rows and rules the item
# reaches and ... the lifespans of the things at the keys it reads (LANGUAGE §4.6 step 5)"; L §4.3: a window at reads
# the def once per class, "If all give one value, that is the value; otherwise it is HOLE-IMPRECISE". city has no
# row: c[ola] is HOLE-UNGOVERNED inside ola's life (to 2026-06-15) and none after (L §4.6 step 5), so a window across
# the end holds two classes with different values: HOLE-IMPRECISE (q3; snap11 let the holes win, a hole of six
# questions). windows each (q4) splits at the lifespan's end; on the days inside it each day's hole names its own law
# date (L §4.6 step 5, `no value at <law date>`), so the answer is not constant there (L §4.4), against E §3.2's "Every
# law date inside one interval gives the same value" (a contradiction in the sixth pass's report; a window inside the
# stretch is REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED, L4_3_at_window_gap_holes).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
kind persons
input city[p in persons]: text
input w: date

def c[p in persons]: text at w
  rule r = city[p]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ola] lives 1950-01-01..2026-06-15
  w = window(2026-06-10, 2026-06-20)

ask q3: c[ola]
ask q4: c[ola] windows each
=== expect
q3: ?"date within window(2026-06-10, 2026-06-20) not precise enough for the law date of c" (c[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-10]: ?"city at ola: no value at 2026-06-10" (city[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-11]: ?"city at ola: no value at 2026-06-11" (city[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-12]: ?"city at ola: no value at 2026-06-12" (city[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-13]: ?"city at ola: no value at 2026-06-13" (city[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-14]: ?"city at ola: no value at 2026-06-14" (city[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-15]: ?"city at ola: no value at 2026-06-15" (city[ola])
  cut 2026-12-31
q4 [w = 2026-06-16 .. 2026-06-20]: none
  cut 2026-12-31
